Ha ha!
Ha ha!


00:28:48.140 --> 00:28:50.480
Just cut the line
and let him go.


00:28:50.970 --> 00:28:51.970
No, just cut...


00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:54.370
Cut--cut--


00:28:54.360 --> 00:28:55.690
Do you want to wander around
with a hook in your face?


00:28:55.700 --> 00:28:57.740
No, other side
of it, man.


00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:00.240
Oh.


00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:05.240
Fly away, buddy.


00:29:05.710 --> 00:29:06.750
All right.


00:29:06.740 --> 00:29:09.620
That lady said
that you put bi--


00:29:09.630 --> 00:29:11.470
She said you put
bread on a string


00:29:11.460 --> 00:29:13.460
to catch a bird?


00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:14.960
Dude, I used to do
this shit in school
all the time.


00:29:14.960 --> 00:29:16.460
Yeah?


00:29:18.470 --> 00:29:19.980
Really?


00:29:21.640 --> 00:29:23.650
MAN: There's too much
anger in this town.


00:29:23.640 --> 00:29:25.000
There's too much fear.


00:29:25.010 --> 00:29:28.430
I mean, this is
the epitome of greed
right here,


00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:29.850
and that's why I want
to leave.


00:29:29.850 --> 00:29:31.320
It's not kind
to outsiders,


00:29:31.810 --> 00:29:33.310
I can see the reaction
of people.


00:29:33.320 --> 00:29:35.160
They look at me like
I'm an illegal alien.


00:29:35.150 --> 00:29:36.520
I think Williston
could be


00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:39.020
one of the best things
to ever happen to you.


00:29:39.020 --> 00:29:41.020
I do.


00:29:41.020 --> 00:29:42.520
Uh...


00:29:42.530 --> 00:29:44.330
Don't give up.


00:29:44.330 --> 00:29:45.620
I think I'm
beyond redemption.


00:29:46.110 --> 00:29:47.190
I don't think reading
a few bible verses


00:29:47.200 --> 00:29:49.290
and hanging out
with some people
in church


00:29:49.280 --> 00:29:50.280
is gonna change
all that.


00:29:50.780 --> 00:29:51.780
But that's just me.


00:29:51.780 --> 00:29:53.780
No, you know what?
Do you know what?


00:29:53.790 --> 00:29:55.290
What, someone's gonna
adopt me and say,


00:29:55.760 --> 00:29:57.300
"Paul, we're gonna
graft you in here,


00:29:57.290 --> 00:29:58.790
you're like my family"?


00:29:58.790 --> 00:29:59.790
I don't think
that's gonna happen.


00:29:59.790 --> 00:30:01.260
I think this is
fantasyland.


00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:02.790
I live in reality,
in the real world.


00:30:02.800 --> 00:30:05.300
What about people
just loving you?


00:30:05.300 --> 00:30:06.810
When is that
gonna happen?


00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:08.300
I'm in my 40s now.


00:30:08.300 --> 00:30:09.300
When's that
gonna happen?


00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:11.720
I know this sounds
so hokey.


00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:14.390
But I want to love you.
I love you.


00:30:17.110 --> 00:30:18.860
But what is here for me?


00:30:18.860 --> 00:30:20.780
I am.
Opportunity? Employment?


00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:23.610
I know.
I am.


00:30:23.620 --> 00:30:25.460
You can come and have
a meal with my family.


00:30:25.950 --> 00:30:27.450
I don't think your wife
likes me, by the way.


00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:28.450
What?


00:30:28.450 --> 00:30:30.290
I sense it.


00:30:30.290 --> 00:30:31.570
I don't think
you should have me
over to your home.


00:30:31.570 --> 00:30:33.070
You might want to talk
to your wife--


00:30:33.080 --> 00:30:34.580
Why not?
Of course I want--


00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:35.580
We always have people
over at our home.


00:30:35.580 --> 00:30:37.090
You have to think about
your family first.


00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:39.580
You're a family guy.


00:30:56.100 --> 00:30:57.560
Hi.


00:30:57.570 --> 00:30:59.610
Hi. Who would I speak
to about an application


00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:02.100
for a truck driver?


00:31:02.100 --> 00:31:03.600
You are a driver?


00:31:03.610 --> 00:31:05.110
Yes.


00:31:05.110 --> 00:31:08.120
How many years
experience?


00:31:08.610 --> 00:31:10.110
About 8.


00:31:10.110 --> 00:31:11.440
Ok.


00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:18.680
I want to see if they have
"Been convicted of any felonies"


00:31:19.170 --> 00:31:20.500
on their application...


00:31:20.510 --> 00:31:22.380
that I've seen so far.


00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:29.690
MAN: It's definitely a place
for a second chance.


00:31:29.680 --> 00:31:31.760
I was at
the Wal-Mart parking lot,


00:31:32.270 --> 00:31:34.780
then the people from Wal-Mart


00:31:34.770 --> 00:31:36.770
didn't want anybody staying
in their parking lot anymore.


00:31:37.270 --> 00:31:38.770
Then I heard people saying


00:31:38.770 --> 00:31:40.610
that they were starting to stay
in a church parking lot.


00:31:40.610 --> 00:31:44.440
Some issues came up
her at the church,


00:31:44.450 --> 00:31:47.240
and then he told me
that, you know,


00:31:47.230 --> 00:31:48.730
I'd have to stay out
in the parking lot.


00:31:48.730 --> 00:31:50.730
He wanted me to
come meet his family


00:31:50.740 --> 00:31:53.160
and that I was
welcome to stay with them
as long as I wanted to.


00:31:53.160 --> 00:31:54.580
So what do you
want to do?


00:31:54.570 --> 00:31:56.570
Do you want to
come over now,
do you think?


00:31:56.580 --> 00:31:58.080
Yeah, let's go over now.


00:31:58.580 --> 00:32:00.050
I don't really know the pastor
personally that well.


00:32:00.050 --> 00:32:03.090
He really doesn't know me
that well, but...


00:32:03.080 --> 00:32:04.580
there's a bond there,


00:32:04.580 --> 00:32:06.050
and there's
a lot of trust there,


00:32:06.050 --> 00:32:09.550
and I guess maybe
it's on a different level.


00:32:09.560 --> 00:32:11.010
He told me that,
you know,


00:32:11.010 --> 00:32:13.520
he thinks that
our two lives came


00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:16.980
and we crossed this path
together for a reason.


00:32:16.980 --> 00:32:18.890
Hi, dear.
Keith is here.


00:32:18.900 --> 00:32:20.410
I'm thinking
it would be good--


00:32:20.400 --> 00:32:21.400
How about if we
brought him over here


00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:22.400
in about 10, 15 minutes?


00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:23.730
Would that be ok?


00:32:23.740 --> 00:32:26.530
I think now
would be better, ok?


00:32:26.520 --> 00:32:27.520
Do you eat
tuna sandwiches?


00:32:27.520 --> 00:32:28.520
Yeah.


00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:30.020
He eats tuna sandwiches.


00:32:30.030 --> 00:32:32.920
Oh, give thanks
unto the Lord


00:32:32.910 --> 00:32:34.280
for He is good.


00:32:34.280 --> 00:32:35.240
Amen.


00:32:35.780 --> 00:32:37.780
And thank you
for good company.


00:32:37.780 --> 00:32:39.200
All right.


00:32:44.090 --> 00:32:46.420
KEITH GRAVES: So, um,
how do you guys feel about


00:32:46.430 --> 00:32:49.300
people coming and staying
in your guys' home?


00:32:49.760 --> 00:32:51.210
When I met him,


00:32:51.210 --> 00:32:53.100
he had an 18-year-old
Native American guy


00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:54.600
living in his basement.


00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:56.600
I forgot about that.
Hmm.


00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:59.050
BOY:
I think it's a good thing.


00:32:59.060 --> 00:33:01.030
It's nice to meet people.


00:33:03.530 --> 00:33:06.400
I think it's good.
I like it. I enjoy it.


00:33:06.400 --> 00:33:10.290
Well, I appreciate
you guys giving me
the opportunity


00:33:10.280 --> 00:33:11.780
to stay with you guys.


00:33:11.780 --> 00:33:12.780
I really appreciate it.


00:33:12.790 --> 00:33:13.740
You bet.


00:33:16.490 --> 00:33:18.740
This is
the family room, ok?


00:33:18.740 --> 00:33:20.570
That's Eric's room.


00:33:20.580 --> 00:33:21.830
This is the laundry room.


00:33:21.830 --> 00:33:23.340
There's the bathroom.


00:33:23.330 --> 00:33:24.740
Anyway, so this is it.


00:33:24.750 --> 00:33:27.140
What made you
decide to...


00:33:27.130 --> 00:33:28.580
let me come
into your home


00:33:28.580 --> 00:33:31.920
and let me stay with
you and your family?


00:33:31.920 --> 00:33:34.220
The first thing
I had to do


00:33:34.220 --> 00:33:35.750
was, quite frankly,


00:33:35.760 --> 00:33:39.770
I was afraid the paper
was gonna come after the church.


00:33:39.760 --> 00:33:43.680
So I had to get you
out of the parking lot.


00:33:43.680 --> 00:33:47.600
I think you bear...
the burden


00:33:47.600 --> 00:33:51.570
of others' injustices,


00:33:52.070 --> 00:33:55.610
but you're not bitter
about it.


00:33:55.610 --> 00:33:57.440
And that impressed me.


00:33:57.450 --> 00:34:01.620
I just thought
this would work.


00:34:01.620 --> 00:34:02.960
Well, let's go in.
Ok?


00:34:02.950 --> 00:34:04.870
Ok.


00:34:04.870 --> 00:34:06.870
JAY, VOICE-OVER:
A sin or a crime,


00:34:06.870 --> 00:34:11.210
while it's real and it is
a part of one's record,


00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:14.540
I would submit ought not be
the definition of one's life.


00:34:16.050 --> 00:34:19.350
I'm not gonna put
my children at risk,


00:34:19.350 --> 00:34:21.850
and I do not believe
that I have.


00:34:35.620 --> 00:34:38.630
Just for now. Huh.


00:34:39.990 --> 00:34:42.870
We're not talking
about Keith.


00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:43.800
Uh-uh.


00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.370
I was gonna call
the elders.


00:34:45.880 --> 00:34:49.890
I decided not
to do that because...


00:34:50.380 --> 00:34:51.880
I don't think I need--
I shouldn't--


00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:53.380
No.


00:34:53.390 --> 00:34:54.890
I don't think
I should tell them yet.


00:34:54.890 --> 00:34:56.900
No, I think that should
just be kept at home...


00:34:56.890 --> 00:34:57.890
Well...
separate from the rest.


00:34:58.390 --> 00:34:59.890
the problem is
if the paper blows it up,


00:34:59.890 --> 00:35:01.890
that's gonna be
the problem.


00:35:01.890 --> 00:35:03.390
But then I guess
I'll have to deal with it.


00:35:03.900 --> 00:35:05.900
And then I'll explain
why I didn't say anything.


00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:08.400
But I don't think
I'd do him a favor


00:35:08.400 --> 00:35:09.900
if I tell
all the elders.


00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:12.350
I don't think
it's right to him.


00:35:12.350 --> 00:35:13.850
It's not, but you
honestly got to


00:35:14.410 --> 00:35:16.920
kind of look at
where your priorities
are, too.


00:35:16.910 --> 00:35:18.410
Well, that's it.
My first priority is to--


00:35:18.410 --> 00:35:21.660
my obligation as a pastor,
but I've got to be careful.


00:35:23.450 --> 00:35:24.950
JAY, VOICE-OVER: You really
have to struggle with,


00:35:24.950 --> 00:35:26.450
what are my motives here?


00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:27.950
I know, I'm...


00:35:29.460 --> 00:35:32.720
Maybe this is
just more self-serving


00:35:32.710 --> 00:35:34.710
than what I realize.


00:35:34.710 --> 00:35:37.710
Maybe it's as simple as
I don't say no very well,


00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:41.970
and so it's easier to say yes
and live with the consequences.


00:36:18.340 --> 00:36:21.850
ENGEL: Well, over
in my makeshift abode,


00:36:21.840 --> 00:36:24.340
I was staying at pastor's house.


00:36:24.340 --> 00:36:26.430
He begged me to stay with him,
which I didn't want to.


00:36:26.430 --> 00:36:29.430
And then after 4 days,
he threw me out.


00:36:29.930 --> 00:36:32.730
He was turning it into,
"I'm throwing you out


00:36:32.740 --> 00:36:34.990
because you don't listen to
my authority" kind of bullshit,


00:36:34.990 --> 00:36:37.500
but he told me the night before


00:36:37.490 --> 00:36:39.490
that he wanted to move in
a sex offender,


00:36:39.490 --> 00:36:40.490
and that's what
it was really about.


00:36:40.490 --> 00:36:41.990
So I confronted him on that.


00:36:41.990 --> 00:36:43.490
I said, "You know,
you're making it about me,


00:36:43.500 --> 00:36:45.500
"throwing me out
for this bullshit reason,


00:36:45.500 --> 00:36:46.460
"but it's really
'cause you want to get


00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:48.500
"the sex offender in your house


00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:51.000
"'cause you're getting heat
from the church where you are,


00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:52.450
"and you're getting heat
from the media,


00:36:52.450 --> 00:36:54.450
and you have to move in here,"
and he admitted that.


00:36:56.960 --> 00:37:00.260
The hypocrisy of the situation
gets me a little upset,


00:37:00.260 --> 00:37:01.510
that someone's gonna tell me
they love me


00:37:01.510 --> 00:37:03.510
and then throw my bags
out in the street.


00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:06.020
I don't know, is that being
true to yourself?


00:37:06.020 --> 00:37:08.360
He told me that he didn't like
my character.


00:37:08.350 --> 00:37:10.140
I mean, one thing about me,
I may be miserable,


00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:12.350
but I'm not living a lie,
you know what I mean?


00:37:14.360 --> 00:37:16.190
I'm not completely
selfish or self-centered
like Keith, though,


00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:18.540
but I am pretty vindictive.


00:37:21.530 --> 00:37:23.480
I told him that,


00:37:23.490 --> 00:37:24.960
"How would you like me
to go knock on every door
in your town,"


00:37:24.950 --> 00:37:26.490
which I haven't done,
"and tell 'em you have


00:37:26.490 --> 00:37:27.990
a registered sex offender
in your house?"


00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:29.990
And I said, "How would you
like me to go to the media?"


00:37:29.990 --> 00:37:32.490
I'll give him a scripture verse.


00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.300
You sew the wind,
you reap the whirlwind.


00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:37.090
Add you're gonna reap
the whirlwind.


00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:42.140
[Piano playing]


00:37:45.640 --> 00:37:47.140
JAY:
I'm kind of a one-trick pony


00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:48.970
when it comes into
reading scripture,


00:37:48.980 --> 00:37:52.320
but there's certain passages
that I just kind of go to.


00:37:52.310 --> 00:37:56.100
This is from "John," chapter 10.


00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:57.430
"I am the good shepherd.


00:37:57.940 --> 00:38:00.450
"The good shepherd lays down
his life for the sheep.


00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:03.820
"I am a good shepherd,
and I know my own
and my own know me


00:38:03.830 --> 00:38:06.170
"even as the Father knows me
and I know the Father,


00:38:06.160 --> 00:38:10.080
"and I lay down my life
for the sheep.


00:38:10.080 --> 00:38:13.280
"My sheep hear my voice and
I know them and they follow me.


00:38:13.290 --> 00:38:16.960
"I give eternal life to them
and they shall never perish,


00:38:16.960 --> 00:38:19.380
and no one shall snatch them
out of my hand."


00:38:28.550 --> 00:38:30.470
That's how we do it.


00:38:30.470 --> 00:38:34.140
They're starting
at $15 an hour here,


00:38:34.140 --> 00:38:35.940
and then they said after
I've been here about 3 months,


00:38:35.940 --> 00:38:37.310
they'll give me a raise.


00:38:37.310 --> 00:38:40.690
I went through being
really depressed, you know,


00:38:40.700 --> 00:38:43.660
'cause I'd been here for about
a month and didn't have a job.


00:38:44.150 --> 00:38:45.980
Just being really happy.


00:38:48.740 --> 00:38:51.130
Mama's happy, too,
my wife's happy, too.


00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:54.370
She was, like, sending me
pictures of the clothes
she had bought, you know,


00:38:54.380 --> 00:38:56.130
and stuff she bought
for the baby that's coming.


00:38:56.630 --> 00:38:59.130
She put a baby bed on layaway,
you know,


00:38:59.130 --> 00:39:00.630
I could tell she was happy,


00:39:00.630 --> 00:39:02.130
and that makes you feel good,
you know,


00:39:02.130 --> 00:39:05.550
that she's getting the things
she wants.


00:39:05.550 --> 00:39:08.050
Hell, this is what I love, too.


00:39:08.060 --> 00:39:09.430
That's what makes it so good.


00:39:09.430 --> 00:39:10.820
I'm doing what I love to do.


00:39:10.810 --> 00:39:12.310
I would have done anything,


00:39:12.310 --> 00:39:15.140
but I'm getting to do
what I love.


00:39:15.150 --> 00:39:19.020
It ain't much to look at,
but it's home.


00:39:19.020 --> 00:39:21.530
I'm glad to be
out of the church.


00:39:24.190 --> 00:39:26.190
I love you, baby.


00:39:26.190 --> 00:39:28.660
I miss you.


00:39:28.660 --> 00:39:31.490
Dear heavenly Father,
we thank you and praise you


00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:34.290
for bringing us to Williston
and for giving us employment


00:39:34.780 --> 00:39:36.280
and providing us with food.


00:39:36.290 --> 00:39:39.290
We praise you in the name
of Jesus Christ, our Lord, amen.


00:39:39.290 --> 00:39:41.630
Amen.
Amen.


00:39:41.620 --> 00:39:42.960
We've sure
been blessed.


00:39:42.960 --> 00:39:45.260
And so we got
pork chops.


00:39:45.430 --> 00:39:48.020
This is where I do
most of my thinking, too.


00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:50.010
I get to bed early.


00:39:50.020 --> 00:39:53.030
I lay here and think about
really how good things
are going right now,


00:39:53.020 --> 00:39:55.020
making money.


00:40:13.820 --> 00:40:16.820
Think about it,
inspector.


00:40:17.330 --> 00:40:20.340
What's up?
Thank you.


00:40:23.330 --> 00:40:26.130
Yeah, that's
a little bit better.


00:40:26.130 --> 00:40:27.380
The thing is
is for the most part,


00:40:27.390 --> 00:40:29.390
it's gonna be your call


00:40:29.390 --> 00:40:31.760
'cause if it looks bad,


00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:34.180
if you think it's bad
and it's gonna fuck
something up...


00:40:34.180 --> 00:40:35.680
All right.


00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:37.150
Tear it up.
It's all you.


00:40:37.150 --> 00:40:39.100
All right.
Enjoy yourself.


00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:42.110
Oh, yeah.
Ha ha.


00:40:54.410 --> 00:40:59.410
My boss got a promotion,
so he's gonna be moving up,


00:40:59.420 --> 00:41:02.430
and the inspector at Patterson
is moving up,


00:41:02.420 --> 00:41:05.420
and they're gonna make me
an inspector.


00:41:05.420 --> 00:41:06.920
Ha!


00:41:07.430 --> 00:41:10.390
They said that it was between me
and another guy,


00:41:10.380 --> 00:41:15.930
and I just kind of had more what
they were looking for, I guess,


00:41:15.930 --> 00:41:19.630
and they were saying
they were gonna hire another guy


00:41:20.140 --> 00:41:21.640
and have him be my hand.


00:41:21.640 --> 00:41:23.640
So I'm gonna have a guy,
I mean, like,


00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:25.140
I don't want to say
underneath me,


00:41:25.140 --> 00:41:27.640
but pretty much.


00:41:27.650 --> 00:41:29.650
It's--Yeah, it's--


00:41:29.650 --> 00:41:33.160
I was just...so...


00:41:33.150 --> 00:41:36.150
Yeah.


00:41:36.150 --> 00:41:37.650
Yeah, I just figured
I'd call dad


00:41:37.660 --> 00:41:41.170
and I thought
I'd let him know 'cause...


00:41:41.660 --> 00:41:45.160
I was...I was real excited.


00:41:50.470 --> 00:41:53.590
