00:55:35.330 --> 00:55:36.830
and you did nothing.


00:55:47.310 --> 00:55:49.810
JAY:
Now he's gonna come after him
in our home.


00:55:49.810 --> 00:55:52.320
He knows that he's in our home.


00:55:52.310 --> 00:55:54.930
[Scoffs]


00:55:54.930 --> 00:56:01.430
I'm glad to give him
a place in my home.


00:56:01.740 --> 00:56:05.530
But what he's gonna do is
by making this a public issue,


00:56:06.020 --> 00:56:09.360
he's gonna make the church
question me.


00:56:09.360 --> 00:56:10.740
[Train whistle blows]


00:56:10.750 --> 00:56:14.620
He's not gonna let it go.


00:56:14.950 --> 00:56:16.530
That reporter...


00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:22.010
could mean the end
of my ministry in Williston.


00:56:22.010 --> 00:56:25.050
That's what it could mean.


00:56:29.050 --> 00:56:31.060
Could mean the end
of everything.


00:56:48.400 --> 00:56:50.400
You ok?


00:56:54.910 --> 00:56:56.910
He knows everything.


00:56:56.910 --> 00:56:59.920
He knows
he's living here?


00:56:59.910 --> 00:57:01.910
Yes.


00:57:14.060 --> 00:57:15.470
I mean, this could be,


00:57:15.480 --> 00:57:17.940
"Pastor, you're just not
competent anymore."


00:57:17.930 --> 00:57:20.060
We'd had a family
discussion about it.


00:57:20.060 --> 00:57:21.480
We've talked about.


00:57:21.480 --> 00:57:23.400
We know the story
of the guy.


00:57:23.400 --> 00:57:25.320
We're very comfor--


00:57:25.320 --> 00:57:26.730
I'm comfortable with him
staying in our home.


00:57:26.740 --> 00:57:28.200
Absolutely.


00:57:32.740 --> 00:57:38.030
JAY: Oh, God, please where
we are tempted to despair,


00:57:38.030 --> 00:57:40.110
give us hope.


00:57:40.120 --> 00:57:42.630
Thank you for giving us
a family


00:57:43.120 --> 00:57:44.950
that is able to share love.


00:57:44.960 --> 00:57:47.300
Amen.


00:58:10.980 --> 00:58:13.480
I thought he was
gonna let it go,


00:58:13.480 --> 00:58:17.990
but he's gonna write
a story, ok?


00:58:17.990 --> 00:58:21.410
If it hits the paper,
the neighbors will know.


00:58:21.410 --> 00:58:24.330
If this goes the way
that you're talking about,


00:58:24.330 --> 00:58:26.290
I'm not gonna be able
to work anymore.


00:58:26.800 --> 00:58:27.810
I'm gonna have
to find--


00:58:27.800 --> 00:58:29.300
You know,
just a second.
Hold on.


00:58:29.300 --> 00:58:30.580
I want you
to stay here.


00:58:30.590 --> 00:58:33.340
I think let's
do this together.


00:58:33.340 --> 00:58:35.260
That would be
my hope.


00:58:35.260 --> 00:58:37.260
What does your wife
think about all this?


00:58:37.260 --> 00:58:40.680
What do you feel
is the best situation


00:58:40.680 --> 00:58:44.410
for your family,
the church, your husband?


00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:47.180
The concerns
I did have


00:58:47.690 --> 00:58:51.200
was the neighbors
and the church


00:58:51.690 --> 00:58:56.190
because people
who don't know
your story...


00:58:56.190 --> 00:58:59.690
uh, can't empathize.


00:58:59.700 --> 00:59:01.210
JAY:
And most people,


00:59:01.200 --> 00:59:02.950
when they hear
"registered sex offender,"


00:59:02.950 --> 00:59:05.450
they think of some--
a molester and a rapist.


00:59:05.450 --> 00:59:06.450
I mean,
they just go on and on.


00:59:06.450 --> 00:59:08.950
And they don't realize,
you know,


00:59:08.960 --> 00:59:12.020
and 18-year-old guy sleeping
with a 16-year-old girl,


00:59:12.510 --> 00:59:15.630
his girlfriend, and that's
a different kind of a...


00:59:15.630 --> 00:59:17.130
but they understand
there's differences.


00:59:17.130 --> 00:59:19.130
I'm concerned about


00:59:19.130 --> 00:59:24.190
the members
of our church, um...


00:59:24.190 --> 00:59:26.190
ah...


00:59:26.190 --> 00:59:30.690
calling into question
my husband's...


00:59:31.200 --> 00:59:33.200
dealings
with the guys.


00:59:33.200 --> 00:59:34.210
JAY: Judgment.


00:59:34.700 --> 00:59:35.700
Judgment.


00:59:35.700 --> 00:59:36.700
What's the whole--


00:59:36.700 --> 00:59:38.150
Let me ask you
this question.


00:59:38.150 --> 00:59:39.700
What's the whole purpose
of the church


00:59:39.700 --> 00:59:41.200
and what's the whole
church doctrine?


00:59:41.210 --> 00:59:43.210
Save sinners,
forgiveness of sins,


00:59:43.210 --> 00:59:44.220
life and salvation.


00:59:44.710 --> 00:59:45.710
That's the bottom line.


00:59:45.710 --> 00:59:46.710
...Christ.


00:59:46.710 --> 00:59:47.710
And then love people.


00:59:47.710 --> 00:59:49.160
...died for
their sins.


00:59:49.160 --> 00:59:50.160
The things that
you guys are saying


00:59:50.160 --> 00:59:51.500
that may be a problem
for the church


00:59:51.500 --> 00:59:52.330
or that the church
is concerned about


00:59:52.330 --> 00:59:53.830
is something
that the church


00:59:53.830 --> 00:59:55.330
is probably supposed
to be doing anyway.


00:59:55.340 --> 00:59:57.230
The problem is


00:59:57.220 --> 00:59:58.590
we're working
with sinners,


00:59:58.590 --> 01:00:00.090
and some people
are fearful.


01:00:04.600 --> 01:00:06.400
JAY: Well, ok,
here's what I'm asking.


01:00:06.400 --> 01:00:09.490
Why don't we, just before
we take any action,


01:00:09.480 --> 01:00:11.480
let's talk face to face.


01:00:11.990 --> 01:00:13.990
At one point
at the previous meeting,


01:00:13.990 --> 01:00:15.500
you were not upset
about this.


01:00:15.490 --> 01:00:17.940
You suggested we get showers
for the men.


01:00:17.940 --> 01:00:22.410
Um, this isn't...


01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:25.410
Anyway, um...


01:00:30.040 --> 01:00:32.130
Yeah, yeah.


01:00:36.340 --> 01:00:39.760
We add new people.


01:00:39.760 --> 01:00:42.350
But it's hard to take off


01:00:42.350 --> 01:00:44.850
the people that
aren't there anymore.


01:00:48.690 --> 01:00:51.190
They left.


01:00:53.190 --> 01:00:55.690
They left.


01:01:01.200 --> 01:01:03.200
They left.


01:01:08.460 --> 01:01:11.630
Well, thanks
for your invitation


01:01:11.630 --> 01:01:13.630
for me to come
and talk with you.


01:01:13.630 --> 01:01:18.550
My presence here tonight
is to just to kind of


01:01:18.550 --> 01:01:20.250
hear what you
might have to say to me


01:01:20.250 --> 01:01:21.300
about what's going on
in your community


01:01:21.310 --> 01:01:23.310
and in your congregation


01:01:23.310 --> 01:01:26.320
and to help me think
if there are ways


01:01:26.310 --> 01:01:28.810
that we as the district
might plug in


01:01:28.810 --> 01:01:30.810
to help you in some way
or another.


01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:32.350
WOMAN: I think the biggest
problem we have right now


01:01:32.850 --> 01:01:34.770
is we've lost many people
from this congregation.


01:01:34.770 --> 01:01:35.770
Uh-huh.


01:01:36.070 --> 01:01:37.400
And I miss them.


01:01:37.400 --> 01:01:39.350
I think when relationships
are put under stress


01:01:39.360 --> 01:01:43.280
by those kinds of pressures,
lots of things happen.


01:01:43.280 --> 01:01:45.200
Does that create
a certain amount of resentment?


01:01:45.200 --> 01:01:46.200
Yes.


01:01:46.200 --> 01:01:47.200
Yeah.


01:01:47.580 --> 01:01:50.160
Do you think the people
of this congregation


01:01:50.170 --> 01:01:53.010
feel like
they are being invaded?


01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:54.840
MAN: Mm-hmm.
I'd say yes.


01:01:54.840 --> 01:01:57.500
There for a while
I didn't feel safe


01:01:57.510 --> 01:01:59.300
coming into
the building.


01:01:59.290 --> 01:02:01.540
Is there any sense
of optimism?


01:02:01.550 --> 01:02:02.970
Is it going to get better?


01:02:02.960 --> 01:02:04.300
Or are you still in a--
Oh, ooh.


01:02:04.300 --> 01:02:06.300
I see heads going already.


01:02:06.300 --> 01:02:07.770
It's not getting better.


01:02:07.770 --> 01:02:10.720
MAN:
It's kind of a twist
in the church right now.


01:02:10.720 --> 01:02:13.020
You can make
all the positive
things you want


01:02:13.020 --> 01:02:14.970
about helping people
and doing that,


01:02:14.980 --> 01:02:19.240
but when we're losing
your people coming
to church,


01:02:19.230 --> 01:02:20.530
are we gonna have
enough people left here


01:02:20.530 --> 01:02:22.280
to take care of
this place?


01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:23.610
The meeting
that we approved


01:02:23.620 --> 01:02:26.910
that we would carry
the overnighters,


01:02:26.900 --> 01:02:28.740
we had 7 new members--


01:02:28.740 --> 01:02:30.650
MAN:
Yeah, I know--


01:02:30.660 --> 01:02:32.970
There was a large manipulation
that went on,


01:02:32.960 --> 01:02:34.830
very large manipulation,


01:02:34.830 --> 01:02:38.330
and I haven't seen
any of those people since then.


01:02:38.330 --> 01:02:40.830
Maybe we're just being used.


01:02:40.840 --> 01:02:44.060
TERRY FORKE:
Please pray for strength
to love each other


01:02:44.050 --> 01:02:46.140
because you are under
extreme pressure,


01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:48.640
and if you depend
on your own abilities,


01:02:48.640 --> 01:02:51.430
you're gonna nose-dive.


01:02:51.430 --> 01:02:52.230
You need to
love each other


01:02:52.730 --> 01:02:54.650
and be able to speak
to each other.


01:02:54.650 --> 01:02:57.560
Our father, who art in heaven,
hallowed be thy name,


01:02:57.570 --> 01:03:00.990
thy kingdom come,
thy will be done


01:03:00.990 --> 01:03:02.450
on Earth as it is in heaven.


01:03:02.910 --> 01:03:06.450
Give us this day our daily bread
and lead us not into temptation


01:03:06.940 --> 01:03:07.860
but deliver us from evil


01:03:07.860 --> 01:03:11.250
for Thine is the kingdom
for ever and ever.


01:03:11.250 --> 01:03:12.610
Amen.


01:03:21.630 --> 01:03:24.520
JAY: Hi.


01:03:24.510 --> 01:03:25.380
How are you
doing today?


01:03:25.380 --> 01:03:26.380
I'm ok.


01:03:26.380 --> 01:03:27.880
Simon Jones
is my name.


01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:28.880
Ok.
I'm from
Mississippi,


01:03:28.880 --> 01:03:30.380
and I
come up here


01:03:30.380 --> 01:03:31.270
to see about
some work.


01:03:31.270 --> 01:03:32.600
Check out job service.


01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:33.600
I plan to do that
in the morning.


01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:35.600
If I can't get
in the oil field,


01:03:35.610 --> 01:03:38.120
then I'll just
head back East.


01:03:38.610 --> 01:03:41.610
Well, um, I'm not
trying to write you
out of the oil field,


01:03:41.610 --> 01:03:45.610
but I will tell you,
age is not gonna be
in your favor.


01:03:45.620 --> 01:03:48.660
Older guys
don't get hired
nearly as quickly.


01:03:48.650 --> 01:03:53.040
Let me give you
the name of a place
in Watford City.


01:03:53.040 --> 01:03:54.320
They're looking
for roustabouts.


01:03:54.830 --> 01:03:56.830
At the very least
it will be worth
a call.


01:03:56.830 --> 01:03:57.840
Hmm.


01:03:57.830 --> 01:03:59.830
Thank you.


01:03:59.830 --> 01:04:00.830
I'm sorry I can't
give you more.


01:04:00.830 --> 01:04:02.660
That's enough.


01:04:17.730 --> 01:04:19.560
You know, it's just
all the phone calls


01:04:19.570 --> 01:04:23.580
and the interruptions
and guys who want help


01:04:23.570 --> 01:04:25.570
and just calling all day.


01:04:26.070 --> 01:04:29.020
So...


01:04:29.030 --> 01:04:31.950
Some days I think
if it were over with,


01:04:31.950 --> 01:04:34.960
it would be better,


01:04:34.950 --> 01:04:39.450
but I also realize
that, um...


01:04:42.370 --> 01:04:45.460
the people are gonna
still keep coming.


01:04:45.460 --> 01:04:47.460
They're not gonna stop.


01:04:47.960 --> 01:04:51.960
And as long as
there's people coming,


01:04:51.970 --> 01:04:56.480
they're gonna be asking
for help.


01:04:56.470 --> 01:04:59.390
And it's hard to say no.


01:05:09.780 --> 01:05:15.820
This is one of the hardest
things we've ever had to do...


01:05:15.820 --> 01:05:18.820
and I'll be glad when it's done.


01:05:47.600 --> 01:05:51.270
Oh, man. Oh, man.


01:05:56.200 --> 01:05:58.590
Oh, my word.


01:06:04.710 --> 01:06:08.100
JAY, VOICE-OVER:
It's damage control.


01:06:08.090 --> 01:06:09.510
Keith is on this list,


01:06:09.510 --> 01:06:16.130
And by putting our church here
as the address...


01:06:16.130 --> 01:06:19.550
I can tell you every neighbor
is nervous tonight.


01:06:24.890 --> 01:06:27.390
Most merciful God
we ask your blessing


01:06:27.390 --> 01:06:30.810
upon the men whose names
appear on the sex offender list.


01:06:30.810 --> 01:06:34.150
Some of those crimes are brutal.


01:06:34.150 --> 01:06:37.030
We ask, O Lord, that you would
help them to know


01:06:37.040 --> 01:06:39.630
that they are not just
what that label says they are.


01:06:39.620 --> 01:06:40.990
When we discovered them,


01:06:41.210 --> 01:06:43.050
they had that...


01:06:43.040 --> 01:06:44.410
Obviously that raises
a concern.


01:06:44.410 --> 01:06:45.910
Pray for the children
that have suffered


01:06:45.910 --> 01:06:48.500
and been abused.


01:06:48.500 --> 01:06:53.330
Pray for the women who
were not treated with respect.


01:06:53.340 --> 01:06:59.020
Please let your word
comfort and guide them.


01:06:59.010 --> 01:07:00.390
WOMAN: No. No, no.


01:07:00.390 --> 01:07:01.890
Ok, well, ok.
It's ok.


01:07:01.900 --> 01:07:03.900
Ok, but just,
you know, ma'am--


01:07:03.900 --> 01:07:05.910
That's fine,
but I don't want any part


01:07:05.900 --> 01:07:09.320
of any more of
all the rigmarole. No.


01:07:09.320 --> 01:07:11.180
[Door closes]


01:07:19.360 --> 01:07:22.860
JAY: I'm kind of sympathetic
with somebody


01:07:22.870 --> 01:07:27.380
who just can't defend
themselves.


01:07:30.870 --> 01:07:34.370
They're carrying burdens.


01:07:34.380 --> 01:07:36.850
Everybody is bearing a burden.


01:07:39.880 --> 01:07:42.220
[Train whistle blows]


01:07:54.450 --> 01:07:56.960
It's just me, it's not my
girlfriend or my kid anymore,


01:07:56.950 --> 01:07:58.950
so...


01:07:58.950 --> 01:08:00.950
She really wasn't liking it
out here.


01:08:00.950 --> 01:08:02.400
I mean...


01:08:02.410 --> 01:08:04.380
I wouldn't like the situation
she was in either.


01:08:04.370 --> 01:08:07.290
She was cooped up all day
in a camper


01:08:07.290 --> 01:08:08.740
watching my son.


01:08:08.750 --> 01:08:11.170
I definitely understand
why it was hard on her.


01:08:11.170 --> 01:08:13.590
That's just
the little things
that come, man.


01:08:13.580 --> 01:08:15.880
She's been
out here twice.


01:08:15.890 --> 01:08:16.890
Twice?
Yeah.


01:08:16.890 --> 01:08:17.890
She try looking
for work?


01:08:17.890 --> 01:08:19.180
Nah, she, uh,


01:08:19.170 --> 01:08:20.970
she's wanting to
get a job back home,


01:08:20.970 --> 01:08:22.970
but it's a lot easier
to get a job back home


01:08:22.980 --> 01:08:24.990
'cause she had my mom
to watch my son


01:08:24.980 --> 01:08:25.980
and her mom.


01:08:26.480 --> 01:08:28.260
I mean, they all
watch him for nothing,


01:08:28.270 --> 01:08:30.070
like they don't ask
no money or like that.


01:08:30.070 --> 01:08:31.580
She needs to be here, man.


01:08:31.570 --> 01:08:33.570
Waitresses are getting paid
16 bucks an hour plus tips.


01:08:34.070 --> 01:08:35.440
You know what I mean?


01:08:35.440 --> 01:08:37.270
This is the best place
to be, man.


01:08:37.270 --> 01:08:38.770
Oh, yeah.


01:08:38.780 --> 01:08:41.750
Really. Well, I mean,
you got to have


01:08:42.110 --> 01:08:43.440
certain tools to survive,


01:08:43.910 --> 01:08:45.950
especially right now
through the winter, bro.


01:08:45.950 --> 01:08:49.420
Well, I ain't ditching
this place.


01:08:49.420 --> 01:08:53.200
What else is there,
man, really?


01:08:53.210 --> 01:08:55.020
I think he just needs
to go see his girl,


01:08:55.010 --> 01:08:56.290
and then he'll
be all right.


01:08:56.290 --> 01:08:57.590
'Cause it's rough out here
with no--


01:08:57.590 --> 01:08:59.540
when you don't have
a female companion


01:08:59.550 --> 01:09:03.610
to help you keep
your level ground, you know?


01:09:03.600 --> 01:09:07.770
When all you see is
males, males, males, males


01:09:07.770 --> 01:09:09.300
hungry for money.


01:09:09.310 --> 01:09:10.810
Mm-hmm.


01:09:10.810 --> 01:09:12.150
Yeah, he'll be back.


01:09:12.140 --> 01:09:13.970
I'm hoping that
I can spend


01:09:13.980 --> 01:09:15.490
enough time
with my family


01:09:15.480 --> 01:09:16.980
and just kind
of see 'em all
and whatnot


01:09:17.480 --> 01:09:18.860
and come back
with a vengeance.


01:09:18.870 --> 01:09:21.740
You know what
you got to do.


01:09:32.710 --> 01:09:35.580
BATTEN, VOICE-OVER:
My wife hasn't talked
to me in about a week.


01:09:35.580 --> 01:09:37.660
She said I've abandoned her.


01:09:37.670 --> 01:09:39.180
I don't know
what's going on.


01:09:39.170 --> 01:09:41.170
She don't answer my calls.


01:09:41.170 --> 01:09:44.550
She's the type of person,
she can't be alone.


01:09:44.560 --> 01:09:48.190
And I've left her alone.


01:09:48.180 --> 01:09:49.980
You know what they say,


01:09:49.980 --> 01:09:52.980
if you don't give them
attention, somebody else will.


01:09:56.600 --> 01:09:59.600
I came out here
with a lot of hope.


01:09:59.610 --> 01:10:02.120
I mean a lot of hope.


01:10:02.110 --> 01:10:04.570
Kind of felt like
it was going good


01:10:04.580 --> 01:10:07.040
just until this last week.


01:10:09.530 --> 01:10:11.950
I mean, if I go home,
I might have a chance


01:10:11.950 --> 01:10:13.450
to get my family back.


01:10:13.450 --> 01:10:15.450
If I don't, I got no chance.


01:10:15.460 --> 01:10:18.520
No matter how much money
I make out here.


01:10:19.090 --> 01:10:23.380
And then when I go home,
what's gonna be there?


01:10:23.380 --> 01:10:26.430
Same ol' nothin'.


01:10:26.430 --> 01:10:28.850
At least out here
I can hold my head up


01:10:28.850 --> 01:10:30.800
and know I'm working
and trying.


01:10:30.800 --> 01:10:34.770
At home, just another bum.


01:10:38.610 --> 01:10:41.900
Coming home, baby.


01:10:41.900 --> 01:10:44.150
Daddy's coming home.


01:10:50.040 --> 01:10:53.040
I wonder how many guys like me
has come out here


01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:54.040
and they're in the same boat.


01:10:54.540 --> 01:10:55.990
They're losing their families.


01:11:00.630 --> 01:11:04.050
It's ironic that I came out here
to save my family,


01:11:04.050 --> 01:11:06.550
and it's probably gonna cost me
my family.


01:11:24.660 --> 01:11:27.120
JAY: I would still ask you
to consider


01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:30.030
that rather than printing
all the name,


01:11:30.030 --> 01:11:34.110
